# goURL project

Postman-like **terminal** HTTP client (Go + tview). Not a web server.

## Packages

- `cmd/gourl` — flags and bootstrap only
- `internal/core` — pure domain (state, store, resolve, HTTP, pairs); no tview
- `internal/ui` — TUI only; call into `core`, never reverse

## Keep in scope

Saved requests, environments/`{{variables}}`, send + cancel, response display (status, headers, body). Match README behavior and keybindings before inventing UX.

## Out of scope unless asked

OAuth, scripting, uploads, nested collections, Postman import/export, encrypting stored secrets.

## When changing behavior

Update README controls/features if user-visible. Prefer Docker Makefile targets for verify: `make test`, `make vet`, `make fmt`.
